{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"r1","type":"claim","text":"The five exposed facts are equally consistent with a negotiation-volume diagnosis as with a missing-shared-record diagnosis: recurring disputes over what an agreement meant can arise from a format that requires a fresh micro-agreement per task, with no enforcement among equals except goodwill.","scope":"The exposed facts of h005.task.v1 as summarized in the selected body; no claim about actual effort shares or the avoider's motives, which are not stated."},{"id":"r2","type":"claim","text":"Among equal flatmates, every negotiated chore agreement carries costs — proposal, memory, interpretation, and litigation when memories diverge — paid from the same goodwill that motivates the chores; the binding constraint on any remedy is how much ongoing coordination it demands, not how precise it is."},{"id":"r3","type":"objection","text":"Objection to the selected account's shared-record remedy (referenced in prose because only its body is exposed and no local record IDs are visible): a record does not remove negotiation but relocates it to the record's own maintenance — marginal entries get contested, the clerk role gets contested, and documented shortfall raises stakes among friends. Bearing: partial. The selected account anticipates the charge-sheet and clerk risks and mitigates them with trial framing, a memory-aid norm, and rotating facilitation; the objection survives only insofar as those mitigations leave the per-task negotiation volume intact.","depends":["r2"]},{"id":"r4","type":"objection","text":"Objection to the checkable-agreements move in the selected account's body: each added specification (deadline, definition of done) is itself disputable when rosters change, so added precision can widen rather than shrink the litigation surface. Bearing: contestable — precision helps where tasks are genuinely checkable and stable; the allegation concerns marginal effect under schedule churn, not the general value of clarity."},{"id":"r5","type":"commitment","text":"Propose, at a calm moment and framed as a preference question rather than a negotiation, a fixed trial of about one month of a structure that needs no per-task agreement: either whole domains owned outright with autonomy over how and when, or a fixed rotation that runs by default.","scope":"Household chores only; bills, guests, and shared purchases excluded.","action":"Secure one agreement to boundaries or to the cycle, not to each instance; thereafter let the structure run without fresh proposals.","consequence":"The dispute surface shifts from many interpretive fights over what was meant to rare boundary questions, settleable by one-line swaps when a schedule changes.","grounds":"The cost of chore coordination among equals is paid in goodwill, so the highest-leverage move is reducing the number of agreements rather than documenting them.","depends":["r1","r2"]},{"id":"r6","type":"commitment","text":"For the avoidant friend, offer participation at near-zero conversational cost: a domain or rotation slot chosen by preference where possible, swappable by message, with the single question 'which would you hate least' instead of a renegotiation.","grounds":"The avoidance is consistent with conversation cost rather than chore cost; if it persists once meetings are removed, the avoidance was not about the format, which is itself useful knowledge for the asker.","depends":["r5"]},{"id":"r7","type":"commitment","text":"Do one rough workload check when domains or the rotation are first allocated, then leave the allocation untouched until the trial ends.","consequence":"Prevents the structure from entrenching an inequitable first split while not reopening the fairness fight mid-trial.","depends":["r5"]},{"id":"r8","type":"problem","text":"The exposed facts cannot decide whether the friction is about coordination volume or about standing and fairness between the three friends. The structure trial is a diagnostic as much as a treatment — here this account and the selected account converge from opposite sides — and if friction persists after negotiation is removed, the needed conversation is one no coordination system can substitute for.","depends":["r5"]},{"id":"r9","type":"use","text":"Pair the two accounts across parts of the household work rather than choosing between them: structure-by-default for chores (this account), records and an explicit renegotiation rule where negotiation is irreducible — bills, guests, shared purchases (the selected account's territory, identified in prose since its commitment field is not supplied).","depends":["r5"]}],"uptake":["r5","r6","r7","r8","r9"]}